WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.940
<i>Stagnate is consumed by 
the desire to kill me.</i>

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.450
<i>We're on even footing.</i>

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:12.980
<i>If I fight him now...</i>

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.880
No! The temple!

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.910
Accelerate

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.350
Acceleratio!

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.680
<i>It was all a bluff!</i>

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.870
<i>He was pretending to be consumed by rage,</i>

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.160
<i>and then he used the cloud of dust...</i>

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.210
<i>It's Blood and Mary that he's after!</i>

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.350
<i>Let me get there in time!</i>

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.390
<i>Please!</i>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.220
Acceleratio!

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.220
Accelerate

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.390
<i>If I can believe what Stagnate says,</i>

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.330
<i>maybe I'm someone he considers 
worth being cautious of.</i>

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.890
<i>But that's not going to mean anything 
to an undead god who can live forever.</i>

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.520
<i>His priority right now is getting 
to Blood and Mary, and then Gus.</i>

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.100
<i>Now that I have the divine protection of the 
goddess of light and can pray for her blessing,</i>

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.770
<i>I can return the three of them to 
the cycle of death and rebirth!</i>

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:04.950
<i>That's what he was being cautious of!</i>

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.700
<i>He weighed Blood and Mary's 
souls against the risk I posed,</i>

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.240
<i>and tried to play the fool...</i>

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.430
<i>That's what I was trying 
to do in the beginning!</i>

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.970
The Faraway Paladin

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.970
Mary! Blood!

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.250
<i>It's no use. I won't get to him in time.</i>

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.700
<i>I borrowed the strength of a goddess</i>

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.140
<i>and finally managed to stand 
on even footing with him,</i>

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.830
<i>but then I fell for a trick like that...</i>

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.020
<i>And now it's all over?</i>

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:11.080
<i>I don't remember seeing her before... but...</i>

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.270
<i>And then everything was clear to me.</i>

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.580
<i>Mary had been forgiven all along.</i>

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.480
<i>She never resented Mary at all.</i>

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.990
<i>Mary never sought forgiveness,</i>

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.710
<i>nor did she expect lenient treatment.</i>

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:41.360
<i>That's why she continued to watch over 
her and admonish her as she wished.</i>

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.290
<i>And she's kept that up for 200 years, 
never revoking her divine blessing,</i>

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:49.610
<i>until Mary could forgive herself.</i>

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.230
<i>What mother wouldn't protect 
an imperiled daughter</i>

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.010
<i>who's devoted her life to worshiping her?</i>

00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:00.400
<i>The earth-mother Mater that Mary 
reveres is truly a great goddess.</i>

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.440
<i>In this moment that Mater has granted me...</i>

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.960
Gracefeel, Goddess of Light!

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.960
Grant this soul peace and guidance!

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:12.860
<i>The Divine Torch guides souls into 
the cycle of death and rebirth,</i>

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.870
<i>but it still can't completely 
defeat Stagnate.</i>

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.510
<i>So what I need to do is...</i>

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:18.470
Wha—

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:19.680
<i>That's right.</i>

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.130
<i>Since these two aren't resisting, the Divine 
Torch will guide them back to that cycle.</i>

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.380
<i>Which means...</i>

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.590
<i>You have to protect them!</i>

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.220
Delay the cycle!

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.600
Flummox the guidance!

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.780
<i>And in the moment when he 
erases my technique...</i>

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.700
Acceleratio!

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.700
Accelerate

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.490
Vasta—

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:47.490
Devastate

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.070
Tacere, Os!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.620
Be Silent, Mouth

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:56.050
You'll start by learning how to use 
minor magic skillfully and accurately.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.800
<i>An exhilarating strike like 
that is far more Gus's style</i>

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.490
<i>than extravagant magic that 
would erase his existence!</i>

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.610
Curse you...

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.780
Curse you!

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:19.310
Will, child of Blood and Mary, 
disciple of Gracefeel!

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.140
I will remember that name!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:26.340
Until you surrender to me, your nights 
will bring you no rest or repose!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.240
That's the kind of thing a 
third-rate villain would say,

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.410
God.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.620
I swear on Gracefeel's light

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.870
that I will never become like you.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:47.880
I will live right...

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.680
and then die.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.320
Search

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.540
Quaerere,

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.170
Ambulare Alevita.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.030
Treading Softly

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.700
Do Not Let Even a Sigh Escape

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.840
Noli Fugito,

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.780
Nor Any Sign of Trembling

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.760
Etiam Sigillum.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.450
<i>That was way too close.</i>

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.580
<i>This Overeater that Blood gave me,</i>

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.750
<i>Gus defeating the double of the Echo,</i>

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:25.630
<i>Mary's earth-mother Mater buying me time...</i>

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.930
<i>All the things that the three 
of them have given me...</i>

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.210
<i>The sword, the magic, 
and the prayer technique,</i>

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:37.400
<i>and most importantly, the part that's 
essentially my core as a person...</i>

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:41.270
<i>If I'd been without any one of them, 
I never would've stood a chance.</i>

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.860
<i>It's all thanks to the goddess's 
divine protection...</i>

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.220
<i>and the three of them.</i>

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.380
Will...

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.370
Will, I'm so glad you're all right.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.480
Mary...

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.660
You did great.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.650
Blood...

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:05.880
You may not share blood, but you are 
still the child of Blood and Mary.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.540
It's only natural that you 
could accomplish this.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.450
Yeah... I did it.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.590
I did it.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.880
<i>I protected them. I'm here 
now with the three of them.</i>

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:23.770
Okay, then!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:27.980
I guess this calls for a party to celebrate 
this victory and Will's adulthood.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:31.270
You're right. I think cleaning up 
here can wait until another day.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:36.400
Well, in that case, we'll have to break 
out the you-know-what from 200 years ago.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.520
You mean that stuff from the dwarfs?!

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.870
You've been hiding something 
like that from us, Old Gus?

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:44.100
Well, it seemed a waste 
to let a child drink it.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.040
What is it? Something tasty?

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.840
So tasty that even I would love to 
drink it, if I had a corporeal body.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.990
Well, you can still fake it, 
can't you? We're celebrating!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.170
Yeah! Drink with us, Gus!

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:55.250
Will...

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.980
Be careful not to drink too much.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.010
If you repeat what happened last time,

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.230
I won't show mercy again.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.230
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.470
That also goes for you, Blood.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:05.990
S-Sure...

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.120
What on earth are you doing?

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.470
Anyway, I suppose I should go and get it.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.960
We should go, too.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:13.800
Yeah.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:18.820
Huh?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.740
Mary?

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.320
Blood?

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.590
I guess we can't after all, huh?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.430
Yes, it seems we can't.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:29.990
But that's how it goes.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.420
We lost our attachment,

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.860
denied selling our souls 
to the god of the undead,

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:36.050
and insisted we wanted to remain undead.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.560
This couldn't last.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.760
Yeah, that's for sure.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.430
I wish we could be spared just one night, 
but I guess that ain't happening.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:47.660
Gracefeel has been exceedingly easy on us.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.200
Under normal circumstances, 
we might have vanished instantly.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.350
What are you guys talking about?

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.170
Listen, Will...

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.330
This is the end for Mary and me.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.620
Y-You're joking, right?

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.630
We're supposed to be celebrating! 
That's just mean!

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:05.500
Will...

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.210
You are a clever boy. 
I'm sure you understand.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.440
Sorry about this.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:15.970
We are sorry.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:20.980
Can't anything be done?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.350
No.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.490
Even if something could be 
done, we mustn't do it.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:30.150
It's like you said. You gotta 
live right, and then die.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:34.030
We got lost for a couple of centuries, 
but you could just call that a detour.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.990
Besides, parents should always 
die before their children.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:41.880
That's the first rule of nature.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.590
Right...

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.990
Yeah. I guess so.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:53.780
But... I'm going to say something I'm 
not supposed to, just this once.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.490
I still don't want to see you two die.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:04.780
I want to see you again when 
I come back here someday.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:09.730
I want to duel with Blood, 
defeat him, and be defeated.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.760
I want us to say silly things to each other.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.260
I want to do chores with Mary,

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.880
and hear her say that I've gotten better.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:20.700
I want you to meet my children 
and grandchildren someday,

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.410
and I want you to teach 
them lots of things, too!

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.540
It's just cruel to say 
you're going away now!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.610
I don't want you to!

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.140
If you two go away, I...

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:34.120
I don't know how I'm supposed to go on...

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.300
Don't go...

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.050
I can't take it.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:41.900
Stay here, even if you 
have to cheat somehow.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.410
Don't be selfish, now.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:52.350
Blood is right. Be reasonable.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.610
First time I've felt like a dad in ages.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:06.880
Will was always a good boy.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.510
Listen, Will. Even if we go away,

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:13.380
humans can live just fine as 
long as they eat and sleep.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.930
You'll find something else to hold dear.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.620
When all's said and done, 
you'll go on living.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:22.080
Once you leave here, 
you're gonna make lots of friends,

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.980
bag yourself two or three pretty girls,

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.380
and have all kinds of fun.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:29.420
Blood! Don't encourage him to be insincere!

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:33.730
Will, you must be sincere 
in love and marriage.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:39.250
Now that you've sworn your oath to the 
goddess of light and killed a god,

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:43.230
the path you walk is sure 
to be filled with troubles.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.700
You will most likely experience setbacks

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.250
and be a target for unjustified criticism.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.250
You may be betrayed by people you help,

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.720
your good deeds may be forgotten,

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.780
you may lose all that you had gained,

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:57.500
and you may end up with nothing but enemies.

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.270
Even so...

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.770
love others.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:03.750
Do good things.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.410
Do not fear loss, build rather than destroy,

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:11.050
forgive sins, offer hope in despair,

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:14.390
and be a source of joy in sad times.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:19.110
And protect the weak from 
violence of all kinds.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:23.400
Just like the way you challenged 
the undead god for our sake.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:25.330
Okay.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:29.080
Oh, Will... William...

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.370
Blood's and my sweet child...

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:38.790
May the divine protection of the spirits of courage 
and the virtuous gods be with you always.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.740
Listen. Move forward with faith 
in the results you'll achieve.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:46.720
Once a person makes up their 
mind, they can do anything.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.790
You might get lost in your 
own thoughts sometimes,

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:52.240
but don't get so stressed 
that you freeze in place.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:57.500
<i>I engraved the images of them and 
the words they said into my heart.</i>

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.880
<i>I won't forget them.</i>

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.300
<i>Just like the light of the goddess,</i>

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:06.030
<i>I know they'll always light my path.</i>

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:08.200
Uh... Ahem!

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.630
Did I get here a bit too soon?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:21.510
<i>After that, we all celebrated 
my victory and my adulthood.</i>

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:24.540
<i>The first drink I had with 
all four of us together</i>

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:29.010
<i>left a lasting impression with 
its strong burn and rich aroma.</i>

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:54.850
<i>That day, the holy light guided my parents</i>

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:57.280
<i>back into the cycle of death and rebirth.</i>

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.180
Yeah.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.290
The view really is the best from right here.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.930
Mary, Blood...

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.340
I know you're not here anymore,

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:16.590
but I'll still come back to let 
you know how things are going.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:20.610
If I make friends or start 
a family, I'll bring them.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:24.670
I'll become an adult who 
can tell you with pride

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.050
that your child is living well.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:32.390
So, for now, I'll be leaving 
you for a little while.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.460
Are you all done?

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:35.870
Yeah.

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:38.260
By the way...

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.420
Why didn't you die, too?

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:44.670
How cruel! You would wish 
death upon an old man?!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.580
Evil grandchild!

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.670
Aw, you're making me sad.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:53.260
I was just thinking all your treasures 
would be mine if you died.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:55.660
You <i>are</i> an evil grandchild!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:58.350
The evil grandchild just outed himself!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:02.710
C'mon, I just meant all the money you have 
no use for would finally have a use!

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:04.580
Right, Grandpa?

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:07.330
That is true. Fine, take it.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:08.140
Huh?

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.180
What is all this?!

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.620
My treasure.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.470
I'll lend it to you interest-free.

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:16.960
Make it grow, you hear?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.260
Er, b-but... I-I mean...

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:22.600
Stagnant money that never gets 
spent might as well be dead.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.850
I don't like stagnant money.

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:26.980
Make good use of it.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:28.250
Gus...

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:32.190
<i>So this is my last gift from Gus...</i>

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:35.180
Not that I'll be passing on for a 
good ten more years, of course.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.010
Huh?

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:40.720
Well, you know, there is still the matter 
of guarding the High King's seal.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:44.030
I made a little deal last 
night with your goddess.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:47.360
She granted me permission to 
continue wandering this city

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.700
for at least ten more years, until the 
god of the undead regains his power.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:51.780
What?!

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:57.050
I have become something like 
Gracefeel's errand boy, it seems.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.710
Th-Then... what about Mary and Blood?

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:03.650
It seems they did not want that.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:08.450
Giving them another ten years would make 
them greedy and reluctant to end it.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.520
If given ten years, they would want 
another ten, then another ten,

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:15.430
and then to remain at 
least until you pass on.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:20.600
They knew they would want that, 
so they chose to die.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:23.530
Just like you, who tried to appear strong

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:27.760
when you were crying and 
screaming on the inside.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:33.730
Granting a position that inspires such 
greed to just one old man is enough.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:36.450
You really are so rock 'n roll, Gus.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:43.030
What will you do with the seal in ten years?

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:46.120
You'll have to figure that out before then.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.900
Huh? You're dumping it on me?!

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:52.420
It seems the worship of Gracefeel has 
gone out of style in the world outside.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:56.800
She used a great deal of strength 
just intervening for us.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:01.680
So the goddess of light's future 
depends on your efforts, as well.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:06.070
I haven't even left, and I keep picking up 
more baggage, both physical and mental.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:09.280
I guess this is one of the hardships 
I'm destined to suffer.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.530
In any case, you'll need money.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.770
Take it, take it!

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:16.820
Yeah... It seems like I'm 
gonna have a lot to do,

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:18.570
so I'll accept it gratefully.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.090
Well, I'm going now.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:46.960
Say, Will...

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:52.010
If you're going out into the world, 
you'll need a last name to go by.

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:57.000
Those two gave you the name "William," 
so I thought I'd give you a last name.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.890
How about it?

00:16:57.890 --> 00:16:59.370
Okay, sure.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:04.890
Then perhaps I'll hijack a custom used 
by certain clans of elves and halflings.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:09.380
They put their two parents' names 
together to form their last names.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.110
Maryblood.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:16.200
You are William Maryblood.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.680
Maryblood...

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:21.480
Take their names with you.

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.010
Thank you, Gus.

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:27.120
I like that name a lot!

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.120
Well, take care.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.080
Indeed.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.520
Oh, and I'll add "G" for my middle name!

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.610
You fool! You don't need my initial!

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.720
What did you learn in 
those classes of yours?!

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.540
Well, you're Gus, after all!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.970
"Old Man Augustus" is just 
too much work to say!

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.720
Hmph. What a hopeless grandson you are.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:53.040
Well, so long, William G. Maryblood!

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.920
Goodbye, Gus! I'll see you again sometime!

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:43.120
Hey, fortress general! Doin' good?

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.350
It's only natural

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:49.700
for two warriors to introduce themselves 
and say a few words before facing off...

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.990
But you demons are just so damn boorish.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:03.970
Being told that by the likes of you 
must leave that demon at quite a loss.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.640
What a mean thing to say.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.860
How's it going on your end?

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:10.050
I performed the funeral quite easily

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:12.020
and stopped the transformation to undead.

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:17.420
Looks like Old Gus's group did just fine.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.950
It appears so.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.610
In any case, we've taken down the fortress.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.940
It won't hurt anything for 
Old Gus's group to retreat.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.100
The fortress general fell 
at the hands of so few.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.380
Any more is just reckless.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:30.340
Don't praise me. You'll make me blush.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.700
I wasn't praising you.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:36.180
How many days will destroying the 
bridge over the Great Canyon buy us?

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:38.220
A few at most.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.680
We're never gonna get anywhere 
unless we take out the High King.

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:43.920
Gus seems to have a plan in mind.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:46.420
Probably still a one-way street, though.

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:48.310
There won't be any way back.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.120
You're not coming.

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:52.680
That's rather sudden.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:56.700
I am a valuable asset in
battle, if I do say so myself.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.190
I know. But you're still not coming.

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:01.770
Seeing you die would make me sick.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:03.780
What?

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:08.290
Couldn't you, at least, add, 
"because I love you," to that?

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.650
It would be pleasing, primarily to me.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:13.370
L-Like hell I'm gonna say 
something that irritating!

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:16.160
You really are hopeless, you know that?

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:18.380
And what if I refuse to stay behind?

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.880
I'll send you back if I have to 
knock you unconscious to do it.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.090
I even got Old Gus's permission.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.850
I see. And I suppose it would 
be pointless to resist.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:28.720
Yeah. Your skills aren't bad,

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.200
but they're no match for the skills 
of the great and peerless Blood.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.800
Then, let's do this.

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:35.640
If you leave me behind, 
I will kill myself on the spot.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.040
Y-You—

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:38.340
Did you not hear me?

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:42.140
I said that if I can't go with you, 
I will kill myself on the spot.

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:43.870
Now, you will take me along, yes?

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:46.140
Th-That's not fair! In a lot of ways!

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:49.090
You may be the strongest man there is,

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:51.570
but no man can win against a woman.

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:53.610
You're so damn stubborn...

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.140
Man, I landed one crazy woman.

00:21:57.140 --> 00:22:00.570
We haven't even done anything, 
and you call me your woman?

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.230
Listen, Mary...

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:04.360
If I make it back alive,

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:07.500
let's find some quiet, 
peaceful place to get married.

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:11.940
Okay.

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:15.660
I would love to.

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:22.860
I'd like a quiet house, 
maybe up on a hill with a nice view.

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:24.070
That sounds lovely.

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.100
I'm sure the breeze would feel nice.

00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:28.160
We could even start a vegetable garden.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:30.250
And if we ever have a kid,

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:32.840
we can ask Old Gus to tutor them.

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:37.420
Despite all that he may say, 
I believe he would agree to that.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:42.240
And if our kid is a boy, 
I'll teach him how to fight.

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:44.310
Between that and Old Gus's magic,

00:22:44.310 --> 00:22:47.250
he'll be the strongest man around, 
even stronger than me!

00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:48.460
How's that sound?

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:52.930
I'm terrified that he would turn out 
to be a very strong, clever failure.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:53.970
Harsh!

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:58.140
So I suppose I'll have to 
teach him the smaller things.

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:00.860
I'm sure our child will be adorable.

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:01.800
Yeah.

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:03.730
What name should we choose?

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:05.390
I've already got one for a boy.

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:07.390
I hope it's not some weird name.

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:09.040
It's a perfectly good name!

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:11.970
Look, we're talking about <i>our</i> kid.

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:14.680
You know he's gonna have an unbending will.

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:19.030
So we'll call him "William," 
meaning "helmet of will."

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:23.880
Episode 5 
The Helmet of Will

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:23.360
William... That's a fine name.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:25.040
I like it, as well.

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:29.160
Will... My little boy.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:39.930
Episode 6
Archer of Beast Woods
